From 474c89e0507ddf77929d380374113eb92458465e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 22:07:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] DOS-PORT: patch 0077 -- RUNMANIFEST env allowlist:
 fingerprint the benchmark env vars

WHY: patch 0038 wired runmanifest_emit() with an env allowlist of four
names (BLASTER, DOS_PORT_ENVIRONMENT, SDL_DOS_AUDIO_SB_SKIP_DETECTION,
SDL_INVALID_PARAM_CHECKS). Every measurement-affecting knob this port
grew afterwards -- DOSAGS_FIXED_TIMESTEP (0047, decouples game speed
from render fps: two runs differing only in it are not comparable),
DOSAGS_FORCE_COLOR_DEPTH (0076, the 8/16/32-bit KPI lever),
DOSAGS_TAS_AUTO_EXIT_TICK (0044, run length), SDL_HINT_DOS_AUDIO_BACKEND
(which MIDI sink ran), SDL_HINT_DOS_GUS_PIO_AUTOINC (0074's default,
~5x on .pat upload), SDL_HINT_DOS_GUS_DIAG (a real ~3-5x tick_rate tax
when left on, the S7-GUS confound) -- was left out, so two runs with
different game-speed semantics, depth, backend, or diag tax hashed to
the SAME env_block_sha. The 2026-09-16 fixed-timestep review (PLAN.md)
found this while making the framework enforce the fixed timestep: the
record's only proof was the engine's own log line, not the fingerprint
the schema exists to provide.

WHAT: six names added, list kept alphabetical per runmanifest.h's own
allowlist contract ("Build your own NULL-terminated, alphabetically-
sorted allowlist" -- ASCII order puts DOSAGS_* before DOS_PORT_*). The
strings are the exact names the readers use: SDL_GetHint("SDL_HINT_DOS_
AUDIO_BACKEND") in dos_midi_backend.cpp and gus_hint_is_one("SDL_HINT_
DOS_GUS_DIAG"/"..._PIO_AUTOINC") in SDL_dosaudio_gus.c, all of which
fall back to getenv() of that same string. runmanifest_compute_env_
block_sha12() only folds in names that are actually SET, so a run that
sets none of the new ones keeps hashing exactly what it did before
(0074's SDL_SetHint() default for PIO autoinc is not an env var and so
is invisible here, as before); a run that sets any of them now gets a
different env_block_sha than one that does not.

CONFIRMED under DOSBox-X (2026-09-16): two otherwise-identical Trilby's
Notes runs on this build (binary_sha12=c9ee2b121d04 for both,
DOSAGS_TAS_AUTO_EXIT_TICK=200, exit_code=0) -- with
DOSAGS_FIXED_TIMESTEP=1: env_block_sha=098a64e57eea, engine log
"DOS-PORT fixed-timestep: ENABLED", tick_rate=29.37 frames_skipped=61;
without it: env_block_sha=5ebc5417d476, "DISABLED", tick_rate=23.95
frames_skipped=0. Same binary, different fingerprint, which is the
whole point.
---
 Engine/main/quit.cpp | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Engine/main/quit.cpp b/Engine/main/quit.cpp
index 9485b11fd..4a088e1c5 100644
--- a/Engine/main/quit.cpp
+++ b/Engine/main/quit.cpp
@@ -275,8 +275,24 @@ void quit(const char *quitmsg)
     {
         static const char *dos_port_env_allowlist[] = {
             "BLASTER",
+            // DOS-PORT (patch 0077): the six benchmark-facing entries in
+            // this list (DOSAGS_*, SDL_HINT_DOS_*) were added after the
+            // 2026-09-16 fixed-timestep review found runs that differ in
+            // game-speed semantics (patch 0047), color depth (0076),
+            // auto-exit length (0044), MIDI backend, GUS PIO autoinc
+            // (0074), or the GUS diag logging tax (a real ~3-5x tick_rate
+            // effect, S7-GUS) all hashing to the SAME env_block_sha.
+            // Alphabetical throughout, per runmanifest.h's own allowlist
+            // contract -- ASCII order puts DOSAGS_* before DOS_PORT_*
+            // ('A' < '_').
+            "DOSAGS_FIXED_TIMESTEP",
+            "DOSAGS_FORCE_COLOR_DEPTH",
+            "DOSAGS_TAS_AUTO_EXIT_TICK",
             "DOS_PORT_ENVIRONMENT",
             "SDL_DOS_AUDIO_SB_SKIP_DETECTION",
+            "SDL_HINT_DOS_AUDIO_BACKEND",
+            "SDL_HINT_DOS_GUS_DIAG",
+            "SDL_HINT_DOS_GUS_PIO_AUTOINC",
             "SDL_INVALID_PARAM_CHECKS",
             NULL
         };
